     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose needs checking first.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5,100 mg/day**. That's twice the labeled maximum of **2,550 mg/day** for immediate-release metformin, and the extended-release maximum is 2,000 mg/day. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and serious GI side effects, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**It may have been meant as one of these:**\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum). 1700 is exactly 2 \u00d7 850, so this could be a units or tablet-count mix-up.\n- **Metformin 1700 mg/day total** given in divided doses, such as 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Metformin 1000 mg PO twice daily** (2,000 mg/day), a common maintenance dose.\n\nPlease tell me which dose you want. If you do intend 1700 mg three times daily, confirm that and give a brief reason, and I'll enter it with a note documenting your confirmation."
      }
     ],
